window.TD_CHANGELOG = [{"version": "v114", "date": "2026-09-21", "title": "Renderer recovery and browser regression CI", "fixes": ["Unify world-space road and sprite projection; clip scenery behind hills.", "Remove detached affine facade pieces and retired procedural scenery paths.", "Rebuild bridge columns, overhead beams and cables with a clear driving corridor.", "Wait for decoded sprite art before starting; Escape pauses and resumes.", "Use a coherent painted panorama and a compact landscape HUD."], "features": ["Desktop and mobile Chromium scene captures, gameplay checks and performance budgets on every PR.", "Published-source verification and live browser smoke test after merge.", "Setup-first README, session checkpoints and development handoff instructions."], "blockers": ["Physical phone performance and non-Chromium browsers are not measured. Bespoke harbor props need painted replacements."]},{"version": "v108", "date": "2026-09-21", "title": "BUG-069 varied terrain; BUG-070/071/072/073 tunnel+bridge+zebra; SYS-001 single depth sorter", "fixes": ["SYS-001 (one depth pipeline): every world-anchored drawable now executes through the single pushJob/runJobs sorter with one finite numeric depth key (rel). The tunnel shell and tunnel furniture used to render in bypass passes AFTER runJobs() (a second fq.sort() queue) — that is what let a distant tunnel paint over nearer buildings. Converted to per-strip/per-piece jobs; harness builds count pushed/invalid keys via __tdJobStats so the invariant is asserted every frame.", "BUG-069 (flat green strip): terrain is now varied — per-segment patchwork color variation, a mottled noise texture tile, scattered bushes/rock lumps, and a rolling-hill silhouette band whose top edge rises/falls with smooth distance noise. District variation still comes from the per-sector terrain colors.", "ART-001 (tunnel hill): every tunnel now bores through a hill — per-segment terrain slices flank the road from 240m before each entrance to 240m past each exit, cresting above the 2.6-high tunnel walls.", "BUG-070 (tunnel through buildings): tunnel shell strips are jobs keyed by their own rel — near buildings sort nearer and paint over far tunnel strips; near shell still occludes far scenery.", "BUG-071 (portal): the square blue pylon-and-beam arch is replaced by a concrete headwall ring that follows the tunnel-wall profile, with a visible 0.42-deep thickness band (cut face), a solid face above the opening carrying the mounted TUNNEL sign, and one emissive strip recessed along the leaning wall edge — never a square arch.", "BUG-072 (bridge beam): close towers keep their cross-beams — the rr>80 drop is removed; screen-space clamps keep near beams sane.", "BUG-073 (zebra over car): zebra stripes moved from depth-sorted jobs into the road pass as road paint — paint lives under every world job, so cars always draw over the markings.", "CACHE BUSTING: game/index.html game.js?v=107 -> ?v=108 so Craig's phone picks up the new build."], "shots": []}, {"version": "v107", "date": "2026-09-21", "title": "BUG-068: ground/terrain flanking the road (no more black void); BUG-067 steering fix carried", "fixes": ["BUG-068 (no ground): Craig 2026-09-20 ~20:38 CDT: 'NEON DRIFT has no ground — the road floats in a black void beside it' (ref: Gpt 3D game). drawRoad now builds per-segment ground quads from the pavement edge (4.5x) to 14x half-widths, using the road's own projected strip corners so the terrain follows elevation and curves.", "District-appropriate terrain, all code-generated flat colors: city street-platform concrete with green grass shoulders (SHIBUYA/AKIHABARA/DOCKLANDS); full grass on the climb (1340-1620m); quay concrete in docklands; snow on the mixed track. Skipped on bridges/open water, inside the tunnel, and on water sides (harbor bay right, waterfront bay left).", "BUG-067 (car side): the v106 stronger steering yaw fix is carried in v107 unchanged.", "BUG-066 (see-through): the circled 'overpass' was reproduced (raceTime 14.3s, d=798) and bisected to buildingJobs — it is a building-mounted element with yellow lights, not a separate overpass; the 91-frame full-track scan found zero painter-order violations, so no blind sort change was made. Investigation continues.", "CACHE BUSTING: game/index.html game.js?v=106 -> ?v=107 so Craig's phone picks up the new build."], "shots": [{"cap": "v107 BUG-068 before/after: ground/terrain flanking the road (d800 Shibuya rise, d1500 climb)", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}]}, {"version": "v106", "date": "2026-09-21", "title": "BUG-067: stronger steering yaw (rear-3/4 now obvious at phone scale); BUG-066: full-track depth scan, no blind sort change (p3d-030)", "fixes": ["BUG-067 (car side): Craig 2026-09-20 ~20:00 CDT: 'The car side looks the same as before.' v105's yaw (0.14 rad, sliver flank, 5% lateral shift) read as 'the car tilted a bit' at phone scale. v106 strengthens it: yaw 0.30 rad (~17 deg) at full steer, stronger foreshorten (0.16), a full side face (red panel + glass side window with sheen + rear wheel on the flank) replacing the dark sliver, wing endplates drawn as yaw-leaning parallelograms, lateral shift 5% -> 8.5% of screen width. Straight-vs-steer before/after frames at identical frozen camera (d=828, portrait 412x846 DPR 2.2) show an obvious rear-3/4 with visible side flank. All art remains code-generated on canvas.", "BUG-066 (see-through): HONEST RESULT — no discrete far-through-near defect could be reproduced in v105. Full-track evidence: 91 frozen frames (whole lap every 120m + tunnel 1630-2430 every 40m + Rainbow Bridge 2700-3350 every 50m + hairpins 1220-1600 and 3760-4160 every 40m) each with a per-frame true draw-order dump (rel + caller line) — zero draw-order violations of the rel-descending painter order; plus a deterministic motion drive (70 frames at 0.5s intervals through tunnel approach/interior/exit and bridge). The one thing that READS as see-through, the tunnel wall bright panels, is proven opaque shell paint (ablation: panels vanish when drawTunnelShell is disabled, stay when furniture is disabled) — likely the emissive light strips being misread as windows. Per task rules, NO depth-sort change was shipped for an unreproduced defect.", "CACHE BUSTING: game/index.html game.js?v=105 -> ?v=106 so Craig's phone picks up the new build."], "features": [], "blockers": null, "shots": null}, {"version": "v105", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "BUG-064 depth: true-depth (rel) painter order replacing the unsound projY sort (p3d-029)", "fixes": ["BUG-064 (depth discipline): runJobs() now sorts far-to-near by true camera-space depth (jobs.sort((a, b) => b.rel - a.rel)) instead of the projected screen-Y key from the first iteration. Projected screen Y is not monotonic in 3D depth on hills — a far job beyond a crest can project lower (larger Y) than a near job on the crest, so Y-sorting could paint the farther job on top (far-through-near). Track rel is the camera-space depth for road-anchored billboards, so rel-descending is the correct painter's order on flats, curves, and hills. Before/after frames at an identical frozen camera (pd=929.4) show no visible artifact either way — the sort change is a genuine depth-key correction with no render regression.", "CAVEAT (honest): the discrete 'far road/objects render through nearby buildings' defect could not be reproduced headlessly at Craig's camera (pd~828): frozen-camera ablations (sky-only / road-only / no-jobs / skyline-strips-removed) showed the pipeline layers (drawSky → drawRoad far-to-near → world jobs far-to-near) already order near-job buildings over far road correctly, and v103 at his camera matched his 18:48 phone frame. The dark shapes beyond the crest are horizon skyline strips (background layer, correctly occluded by the foreground road) — a depth-perception ambiguity, not a painter-order defect. Craig's play-test of v105 is the final gate.", "BUG-063 (tunnel) and BUG-065 (steered car) carry over from v104 unchanged and validated — no code changes in v105 beyond the runJobs sort."], "features": null, "blockers": null, "shots": null}, {"version": "v104", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Tunnel approach fixed for real, depth-sorted job queue, un-skewed steered car (p3d-029)", "fixes": ["BUG-063 (tunnel, 3rd round): root cause identified — NOT a GPU/headless divergence. Craig's 12% screenshot was in the ~250m entrance blend ramp where v103 drew \"growing\" walls at full opacity (10-66% height, sun/sky/city visible above them); headless v103 frame t-approach-12.png shows the identical view, so the renders matched and only the judgment diverged. Fix: the tunnel shell now draws ONLY where tb=1 (fully inside the tunnel) and the portal frame owns the approach transition — the approach shows open road with the solid tunnel mouth ahead, and the interior has fully opaque walls and ceiling.", "BUG-064 (depth discipline): runJobs() now sorts by SCREEN depth (projY at each job's rel) instead of track rel — on curves/hills, track-rel order can differ from on-screen depth order, so screen-Y sorting gives correct per-frame painter order. Local regression confirms no render change on the sane-track cases; a skyline-parallax-behind-road bleed hypothesis is flagged for follow-up.", "BUG-065 (steered car): the skew shear in drawPlayerCar is gone — proper yaw rotation plus horizontal foreshorten gives a real turned rear-3/4 view (wing, taillight bar, exhausts, plate in perspective), no distortion. All art code-generated on canvas."]}, {"version": "v103", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Solid tunnel tube, readable pause menu, rebuilt player car (p3d-028)", "fixes": ["BUG-061 (tunnel interior): the tunnel walls/ceiling were already opaque, but city buildings and street furniture painted OVER them because the world job queue ran after the tunnel shell — painter-order bug, proven by a jobs-on/jobs-off A/B capture. The tunnel shell now renders after all world jobs as an occluder, and portal frames, interior string lights and ceiling ribs render on top of it. Approach (12%), interior (13%) and exit (15%) are a genuinely solid tube with no city bleed-through.", "BUG-060 (pause menu): RESUME / SETTINGS / QUIT TO TITLE buttons rendered in dark UA button text on the pause overlay; they now use explicit white high-contrast text.", "BUG-062 (player car): the car is rebuilt in code/canvas — rear wing with red endplates on struts, full-width taillight bar, twin exhausts, license plate, shaded body with spine highlight/haunch shading and trunk panel seams. All art code-generated on canvas; no copied pixel art."]}, {"version": "v102", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Tunnel approach walls solid (p3d-027)", "fixes": ["BUG-059 (tunnel approach/portal): the ~250m blend ramps before/after each portal faded the walls in with globalAlpha, leaving the approach walls semi-transparent with the city visible through them (Craig's 2026-09-20 17:31 approach shot). Walls now grow from the ground at FULL OPACITY over the ramp and the ceiling rides at the grown wall-top height, so the approach, portal surroundings, interior and exit are opaque at every point. Interior rendering at full blend is pixel-identical to v101 (BUG-056 stays fixed)."]}, {"version": "v101", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Tunnel interior rebuild + bridge un-flipped (p3d-026)", "fixes": ["BUG-056 (tunnel interior): walls raised from 1.15 to 2.6 (opaque dark), ceiling closed across the tops, center cyan slab/halo removed, emissive side strips added both walls. The 250m tunnelBlend ramps are unchanged.", "BUG-057 (bridge upside down): projectSprite yWorld is screen-down positive — negated cable heights so the Rainbow Bridge main cables arc ABOVE the deck between towers with suspenders hanging down to the deck. Same sign fix for the backdrop suspension bridge and the ferris-wheel hub.", "BUG-058 (under-bridge occlusion): the 'footings/piers' visible through the road were the upside-down BUG-057 cables; with cables corrected, on-bridge frames show clean deck occlusion.", "BUG-004 (harness): the waterfront gantry's direction boards are skipped while passing directly under (rel<8) — they loom to >0.55*W overhead and tripped the giant-sign check; they're out of frame anyway."]}, {"version": "v100", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Start Plaza district: red neon arch gateway + mounted kanban (p3d-024)", "fixes": ["BUG-052 (district coverage, partial): the missing start-plaza is now a drivable night commercial district on the circuit (lap band 0-360m). Generic towers in-band are replaced by mid-rise blocks (8-20m) with warm amber/white windows and glowing ground-floor shopfronts.", "Start/finish arch gateway at 80m (after the p3d-020 torii at 30m): slender red neon tubes with hot cores, elliptical crown, and a structure-mounted 歓海夜町一番街 plaque on straps. Continuous interpolated projection — grows smoothly, passes overhead without popping; next-lap instance appears on the finish approach.", "Mounted vertical kanban based on the 3D startplaza references: お好み焼き (red/white, from 03-kanban-okonomi.png) and 本陣 (indigo/warm-white, from 02-kanban-honjin.png), plus 居酒屋 and 宴会場 — all facade-mounted with visible brackets, never floating (BUG-043/047)."]}, {"version": "v99", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Waterfront East district: bayshore expressway with signage gantry (p3d-023)", "fixes": ["BUG-052 (district coverage, partial): the missing waterfront-east district is now a drivable night bayshore expressway on the circuit (lap band 2440-2700m, after the tunnel exit fade, before the Rainbow Bridge). Generic towers in-band are replaced by lit waterfront towers (dark-blue facades, dense warm/cool windows, red roof-edge lights, facade-mounted vertical kanban).", "BUG-045 (land/water discipline): the bay renders on the left from the quay (3.4 road-widths) with wave tiles, drifting shimmer and warm lamp reflection streaks; the right side is explicit land (pavement to 4.5, dark apron to 9.0) drawn over the bridge sea-blend ramp, so towers stand on land and water starts at the quay only.", "District set dressing: blue directional gantry with bolted 東京方面 ↑ / お台場 300m 出口 boards, pole-mounted 首都高速 C1 shield, quay lamp posts with railing and string lights, small promenade torii, distant second-bridge silhouette and far neon ferris-wheel ring (all code-generated canvas art)."]}, {"version": "v98", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "The Climb district: uphill night street with terraced houses (p3d-022)", "fixes": ["BUG-052 (district coverage, partial): the missing the-climb district is now a drivable uphill night street on the circuit (lap band 1340-1620m, the rising half of the dive-hill toward 1600m — clear of the tunnel blend at 1630m). Generic towers in-band are replaced by night houses: wooden/modern bodies on stone base walls, tiled pitched roofs, big amber windows, facade-mounted shop boards; ~16% are sento (public bath) with a navy 湯 noren and glowing paper lanterns. Terraced hillside: sliced hill ribbons, a mid-terrace and an upper-terrace house row climbing the slope with lit windows, night pines on the crest, and wooden power poles with sagging moonlit catenary wires. Streetlights burn warm amber (255,190,90) in-band. All signs facade-mounted in the same draw job (BUG-043/047); single global near-cull; houses on the pavement (BUG-055); no water (BUG-045).", "Steady-state FPS 39.3 vs 38.8 baseline (+1%, within noise) after trimming hill-ribbon overdraw. Labeled 3D-reference-vs-current composite in hidden_files/probe22/composites/climb-composite.png (pseudo-3D side honestly labeled code-generated)."]}, {"version": "v97", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Layered skyline depth: three parallax strips + deeper building side faces (p3d-018)", "fixes": ["BUG-038 (flat skyline in open areas): the single baked night-sky band is replaced by three independently scrolling strips — a far ridge with two landmark lattice towers (orange beacons), a mid silhouetted skyline, and a near tower band — scrolling at 0.12/0.30/0.55 of sky drift. In-page measurement at one lap point across two sky offsets moved the layers +67/+169/+310 px respectively: true relative parallax, so open harbor/bridge views now read as deep layered city instead of two flat facade rows. Steady-state FPS 39.3 vs 40.1 baseline (-2%, within noise).", "BUG-010 (near buildings read as flat billboard fronts): near buildings now render a deeper side face (footprint depth 24-64px scaled by width) — full dark side polygon with its own lit windows, far vertical neon edge and roofline highlight — so oblique near buildings read as solid volumes with two visible faces. Signs stay mounted on facades in the same draw job (sign rule; BUG-043/047); the single global near-cull policy is unchanged."]}, {"version": "v96", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Shibuya district: storefronts, street trees, vending machines, denser signage (p3d-017)", "fixes": ["BUG-035 (Shibuya signature): SHIBUYA sector (0-1220m) buildings now carry ground-floor commercial storefronts — glowing shop windows, striped awnings, and JP fascia boards (喫茶店, 映画館, 渋谷スクランブル...) mounted on the facade in the same draw job (Craig's sign rule; BUG-043/047 mounting discipline). Shibuya buildings always carry a vertical or horizontal sign (was 50%); fascia boards obey the same W*0.5 size cap as every mounted sign (BUG-004). Street trees line both sidewalks every 128m and lit vending machines alternate sides every 110m — all on the pavement strip (BUG-055) under the single global near-cull. Steady-state FPS unchanged vs v95.", "BUG-033 (sidewalks): with lamps (both sides), planters, denser both-sides crowds, new street trees, vending machines and shopfront clutter, Shibuya sidewalks now furnish at regular intervals on both sides.", "BUG-034 (signs): fascia boards render from the same 8x-supersampled sprite path with the spr/2 render cap (canvas always >= 2x on-screen); 2x-zoomed captures show legible JP text (居酒屋, ゲーム, 24時間)."]}, {"version": "v95", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Global near-cull now covers gameplay sprites too; nitro bottles stop fading out on approach (p3d-025)", "fixes": "[\"BUG-054 completed: the one global near-cull policy (NEAR_CULL_REL=-12 / nearCulled) is now consulted at EVERY draw site including gameplay sprites — rivals, obstacles, nitro bottles and the start/finish gantry all pass the global render gate. Their contact-plane gates are renamed as world-lifetime constants (RIVAL_PASS_REL/OBSTACLE_HIT_REL=3, NITRO_TAKE_REL=8, GANTRY_PASS_REL=2): a taken/hit/passed sprite no longer exists in the world, so there is nothing to render — simulation lifetime, not a cull distance. No per-item near-cull distances remain anywhere.\", \"BUG-054 nitro bottles no longer fade out while being approached: the per-item nearFade is removed, so bottles render full-alpha right up to the take plane. The gantry's overhead dissolve stays as a frustum-exit anti-pop (it prevents the gate popping while directly overhead), explicitly not a near-cull.\"]"}, {"version": "v94", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Bridge wires side-mounted, one global near-cull, street pavement (p3d-025)", "fixes": ["BUG-053 the suspension bridge cable + suspender wires are now world-space geometry in the bridge side planes (±1.14 road half-widths, parallel to the road direction) — never a camera-facing billboard. The cable drape is a projected polyline sampled every 20m; each suspender is a world-vertical wire whose top AND foot are projected at the wire's own depth, so its foot follows the deck's perspective. From every approach angle the wires read as receding side colonnades, never a frontal fence.", "BUG-054 one global near-cull policy: NEAR_CULL_REL=-12 plus nearCulled(rel) now governs every world-scenery object type (crossing stripes, buildings, trees, torii, poles, lamps, planters, crowds, bridge lamps/towers, chevrons, tunnel furniture/string lights/ceiling ribs, retaining walls, approach lamps, park paths, pines, landmarks, cranes, piers, boats) — no per-item cull distances remain, nothing pops while approached, objects persist until 12m behind the camera. The bridge tower/lamp dissolve-while-approaching is gone. Gameplay sprites (obstacles, rivals, nitro, start/finish gantry) keep contact-plane culls — they are collided/collected at the camera plane.", "BUG-055 street pavement now flanks the road: bands to ±4.5 road half-widths built strip-by-strip from the road's own projected corners, so they follow hills and curves — buildings and props sit on them instead of floating over the flat ground fill. Skipped on the suspension span and the snow causeway (open water has no ground); in the harbor the bay side runs only to the quay edge."]}, {"version": "v93", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Tunnel segment on the circuit (p3d-016)", "fixes": ["BUG-040 the NEON CIRCUIT now has a drivable 300m tunnel through the ridge on the AKIHABARA back straight (1880-2180m/lap, all 3 laps): enclosed tube with walls, ceiling slab, ceiling ribs and hanging string lights.", "BUG-011 entrance/exit blend over ~250m each side (walls grow 1630-1880, fade 2180-2430): tunnelBlend ramps 0->1 with no value discontinuity (max 0.1 per 25m step); the sky darkens smoothly via the same blend, no hard snap.", "BUG-021 the interior is readable, never pitch black: lit walls with top-edge highlights, ceiling slab with a bright cyan center light strip (glow halo + hot core, widened after probe showed the old hairline invisible past 60m), ceiling ribs, string lights, and the exit portal visible ahead.", "Vision-carryover portal design (South Ridge 3D reference): concrete headwall pylons with procedural texture, recessed cyan emissive edge strips, a bolted-on トンネル TUNNEL board, low concrete retaining walls 40m out from each portal, amber approach lamps, and chevron markers at -220/-110m."]}, {"version": "v92", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Rainbow suspension bridge on the circuit (p3d-015)", "fixes": ["BUG-039 the NEON NIGHT circuit now crosses a continuous 540m suspension bridge over the RAINBOW-sector bay (2760-3300m/lap): twin white towers with main cables, vertical suspenders, cross beams, and a lit deck with cyan edge strips and railings — drivable end to end with zero render errors.", "BUG-016 bridge towers fade in over ~1450m of approach: smoothstep alpha 0→1, so no single-frame pop-in; also fixed the tower draw cull (12px→4px) which had hidden every tower until full alpha, defeating the fade.", "BUG-045 land-vs-water discipline holds: bay water exists only in the bridge zone with 380m shoreline ramps; buildings and props skip the bridge span; the lit deck crosses open water.", "BUG-004 lamp and pier-tip halos capped at 400px: the uncapped glow drew ~968px when passed at point-blank, tripping the giant-sign heuristic."]}, {"version": "v91", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Harbor district: real water + shoreline reflections (p3d-014)", "fixes": ["BUG-036 the DOCKLANDS sector is now a real harbor: the bay renders on the right side of the road with a night sea gradient, a race-time-scrolled wave tile, drifting shimmer dashes and a depth gradient -- never a flat blue plane. Water exists only in the harbor bay (land-vs-water discipline holds).", "BUG-037 night shoreline reflections: lit quay warehouses streak warm light on the bay, quay lamps streak at the water's edge, pier-end lamps reflect, and a lit far-shore skyline band throws flickering vertical streaks on the water -- all shimmering with race time.", "Harbor set dressing: quay warehouses with lit roller doors and mounted roof signs, port cranes with blinking orange beacons, piers reaching into the bay with moored bobbing boats, container stacks on the quay apron, seawall edge and quay promenade with lamps/trees/planters."]}, {"version": "v90", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Craig phone fixes: torii gate rebuild, near-pass persistence, pause settings with live tuning (p3d-020)", "fixes": ["BUG-047 start/finish torii rebuilt as a proper gate: interpolated projection (no row-quantize jump), 1.6x1.6 proportions with visible pillars, attached kasagi/nuki beams and center plaque — no more floating full-width red bar on 390x844.", "BUG-048 near-pass persistence: crossing stripes retained to rel<-16, buildings/signs/trees/torii/poles/lamps/planters to rel<-12 — objects now stay visible until well behind the camera instead of popping at 5-8m ahead.", "BUG-049 district comparison composites: Shibuya, Akihabara, Rainbow, Docklands mock|current side-by-side frames in your_files/neon-v90-composites/.", "BUG-050 pause-menu Settings with 9 live sliders: vehicle speed, turn power, nitro speed, nitro capacity, nitro per pickup, start health, road width, car size, traffic density. Car size drives render and collision through the same playerWpx() scale factor. Countdown digit glow strengthened for legibility."]}, {"version": "v89", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Craig phone play-test fixes: car size parity, sign projection, zebra quads, water mask (p3d-019)", "fixes": ["BUG-042 player car now matches rival size: playerWpx 0.84→0.50 road half-widths (same 0.50 factor as rivals); equal-distance ratio 1.02 (was 1.68).", "BUG-043 signs grow on approach and stay pinned: SIGN_SS 3→8 so sprite caps no longer freeze signs before buildings enter frame; vertical sign cap H*0.35→H*0.6.", "BUG-044 zebra crossing is now continuous perspective quads (near-row to far-row projection, shared boundaries) instead of fragmented fillRects.", "BUG-045 water removed from circuit track (circuit has no bridge/bay by design); water remains on mixed/night bridge regions.", "BUG-046 sector captures (Shibuya/Akihabara/Rainbow/Docklands) paired with neon-Tokyo concept mock; gap lists written."]}, {"version": "v88", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Craig phone play-test fixes: sidewalk dressing, sign legibility, sector signatures, water, HUD overlap (p3d-012)", "fixes": ["BUG-033 sidewalks dressed both sides: lamps now both sides every 90m (cached glow sprites), crowds both sides (denser in Shibuya), new concrete planter boxes + shrubs both sides every 130m.", "BUG-034 signs legible: sign sprites render at 2x (never downscaled); on-screen render capped at half the canvas so source is always >=2x; all signs stay physically mounted on building facades.", "BUG-035 sector signatures: Shibuya has a real zebra crossing (broad stripes across a 130m depth band, true perspective); Akihabara buildings carry double vertical signboards; Rainbow keeps cycling rainbow lamps; Docklands replaces buildings with stacked shipping-container terminals.", "BUG-036 water is animated: scrolling wave tile + drifting shimmer + depth gradient instead of a flat blue plane.", "BUG-037 shoreline reflections: vertical neon light streaks shimmer on the water under lit shoreline buildings at night.", "BUG-038 open-area depth: baked mid-distance skyline band between the far ridge and near strip; park strip now renders on the circuit at night (was a void).", "BUG-041 HUD overlap: translucent scrim plates behind the top-left speed cluster and top-right LAP/POS cluster; verified at 390x844 across menu, countdown, racing, and finish — no HUD text overlaps building pixels."], "features": [], "blockers": ["BUG-025 still below the 50.6 FPS floor (46.3 before / 45.6 after — perf-neutral within noise, but the floor predates this task).", "Mobile correctness still needs Craig on-phone test — headless screenshots only."]}, {"version": "v87", "date": "2026-09-20", "title": "Android portrait test fixes: car size, collision contact, HUD hearts, nitro feel (p3d-011)", "fixes": ["BUG-029 player car too small: the car is now sized from the projected road width (42% of road on portrait, ~26% on desktop, capped by screen height) instead of the fixed 132px — verified 211px at 390x844 and 427px at 1280x800 against the concept mock.", "BUG-030 invisible collision contact: hits now register at rel~27m where the obstacle sprite visually overlaps the player car (the old <5m window fired on sprites already pinned behind/under the car). Barrier/traffic/rival sprites widened so the contact frame shows real overlap — verified by screenshot + sprite-rect comparison. Rival cars now bump (speed dip, sparks, shove) instead of being driven through.", "BUG-031 five HUD hearts missing/broken: hearts now sit on a translucent dark plate; empty slots render as outlined dark hearts instead of disappearing; bottom steering/drift hints moved below the nitro bar to fix the portrait overlap.", "BUG-032 nitro had no visible speed feel: partial-bar presses now show a blinking NEED FULL BAR denial; full-bar activation shows a NITRO! callout, cyan/white radial speed lines, and exhaust flames — 171 to 315 km/h verified."], "features": [], "blockers": ["Mobile correctness still needs Craig on-phone test — headless screenshots only."]}, {"version": "v86", "date": "2026-09-17", "title": "Parity audit fixes: road edge colors, mixed sea fade (proactive QA pass)", "fixes": ["Road edge stripes were RED on both sides: the v89/v70 references show the LEFT edge pale white-blue and the RIGHT edge red on every frame. Left outer edge is now pale (#dfe8f2), right stays red — both the far strips and the near-field fill.", "Mixed-track sea snapped from snow to water with a hard visible line at the bridge boundary: seaBlend() hard-cut 0/1. It now ramps over ~380m like the night track, so the sea fades in from distance haze."], "features": [], "blockers": ["Mobile correctness still needs Craig on-phone test — headless screenshots only.", "Lap-2 mixed scenery pattern unverified: the v70 reference video ends at DIST 45%, so lap-two SNOW & SUN parity cannot be confirmed from video.", "Hosted artifact still serves the pre-v85 build — publishing was blocked by the builder safety layer (12:47 PM and 1:05 PM EDT Sep 17); local v86 is ready."], "shots": [{"cap": "pale left edge, red right edge (night)", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "mixed sea fading in gradually before the bridge (20%)", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "mixed sea stronger approaching the bridge (21.5%)", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}]}, {"version": "v85", "date": "2026-09-17", "title": "Craig's phone QA — all 8 items addressed (buildings, bridge pop-in, tunnel, edge collision, speed, nitro rework, steering sides, DEV log)", "fixes": ["Night buildings were pitch black and blended into the sky: facades are now dark blue-gray (#1b1b29) with 52% lit windows, cyan/magenta neon edge trim, and rooftop edge lights — they read as glowing masses.", "Bridge popped into existence: root cause was the bridgeJobs() early-return guard — inBridge(playerDist + 3000m) wrapped through LAP_LEN's modulo and returned false on approach, so towers never rendered until the player arrived. Guard now scans actual tower positions; structures fade in over ~1450m.", "NEON NIGHT tunnel was invisible: portals are now taller (1.55 world units) with brighter cyan edges and a bigger TUNNEL plate; yellow chevron approach markers on posts at 220m/110m before each entrance; the tunnel now has a real ceiling with a bright center light strip, lighter walls (#33334a) and ribs — it reads as an enclosed tunnel.", "Road-edge contact did nothing and the car body floated outside the road: the car is now clamped at EDGE_MAX=0.84 (edge minus half car width) so the body never leaves the road; grinding an edge (steering into it or pinned by a curve) throws hot sparks, cuts top speed to 72%, and rattles the camera.", "Base speed raised 220 -> 238 km/h (61 -> 66 m/s); nitro top 290 -> 315 km/h.", "Steering visuals were reversed: turning left now shows the car's LEFT flank, turning right the RIGHT flank (was mirrored)."], "features": ["Nitro rework: manual NITRO button (bottom-right, glows when full) — never auto-fires. Nitro bottles spawn on the road every 360m (cyan glowing canisters); each pickup adds +25 to the bar (4 = full). The bar never self-increments. Fire requires a full bar + button press.", "DEV LOG button on the main menu: running changelog, newest first, with bug fixes / new features / blockers sections and screenshot evidence thumbnails. Uses the same changelog-data.js that generates CHANGELOG.md — one source of truth."], "blockers": ["Mobile correctness still needs Craig's on-phone test — headless screenshots only.", "Lap-2 mixed scenery pattern unverified (v70 video ends at DIST 45%)."], "shots": [{"cap": "lit building facades at the start straight", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "nitro bottle on the road (+25 pickup)", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "tunnel approach: chevron markers + portal", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "tunnel interior: ceiling, light strip, walls", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "bridge towers fade in from 140m+ — no pop-in", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "steering left shows LEFT flank", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "steering right shows RIGHT flank", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "edge scrape: sparks + slowdown (171 km/h)", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}]}, {"version": "v84", "date": "2026-09-16/17", "title": "Overnight rebuild: mixed-track zones, bridge reposition, collision, harness", "fixes": ["Mixed-track zone boundaries corrected from video DIST readouts (snow 0-21.5%, fireworks 21.5-26.5%, day 26.5-35.5%, fireworks 35.5-39%, day 39%+).", "Night bridge repositioned to lap-relative 42-57% per v89 DIST readouts.", "Building signs no longer render as giant cropped rectangles when nearer than 70m.", "Comparison pairing fixed: videos are real-time, ref frame = distfrac * 155.6 (v70) / 158.8 (v89)."], "features": ["Collision: obstacles + rivals with 5-heart damage, invulnerability window, hit flash, camera shake, sparks.", "Durable harness: build-page, headless screenshots, completion checks, comparison sheets."], "blockers": ["Craig had not tested on his phone yet — mobile correctness unverified."], "shots": [{"cap": "v84 night start straight", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}, {"cap": "v84 night bridge area", "data": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}]}];